WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.734
Safe file handling is the discipline of controlling how Python
applications receive, name, store, read, write, process, serve, and delete
files.

2
00:00:08.734 --> 00:00:17.327
That includes web uploads, API attachments, command-line scripts, data
pipelines, automation jobs, background workers, and internal tools.

3
00:00:17.327 --> 00:00:25.286
A file operation may look simple in code, but it can affect
confidentiality, integrity, availability, auditability, and user trust.

4
00:00:25.286 --> 00:00:29.724
File handling is security-sensitive because files carry more than bytes.

5
00:00:29.724 --> 00:00:32.400
A filename may influence storage decisions.

6
00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:34.654
A path may cross a directory boundary.

7
00:00:34.654 --> 00:00:37.190
Metadata may reveal private information.

8
00:00:37.190 --> 00:00:40.148
Permissions may expose data to the wrong process.

9
00:00:40.148 --> 00:00:43.106
File contents may be parsed by complex libraries.

10
00:00:43.106 --> 00:00:50.009
Downstream processing may transform, index, preview, scan, export, or
serve the file in a different trust context.

11
00:00:50.009 --> 00:00:57.827
It helps to distinguish filenames, paths, file contents, metadata,
permissions, storage locations, and downstream processing.

12
00:00:57.827 --> 00:01:00.293
A filename is a label, not proof of safety.

13
00:01:00.293 --> 00:01:03.674
A path is an instruction about location, not merely text.

14
00:01:03.674 --> 00:01:06.914
Content type and extension are hints, not guarantees.

15
00:01:06.914 --> 00:01:09.872
Storage location controls who can reach the file.

16
00:01:09.872 --> 00:01:14.239
Processing determines what the application later does with the content.

17
00:01:14.239 --> 00:01:16.422
Files often cross trust boundaries.

18
00:01:16.422 --> 00:01:20.649
A user upload moves from an untrusted client into server-side storage.

19
00:01:20.649 --> 00:01:24.100
A scheduled job may process files dropped by another team.

20
00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:27.551
A data pipeline may parse documents from a partner system.

21
00:01:27.551 --> 00:01:32.763
Safe file handling is therefore part of application design, not only input
validation.

22
00:01:32.763 --> 00:01:38.680
The goal is to make file operations explicit, bounded, authorized,
observable, and maintainable.
